# AI PalmPilot (agent_palm)

> **Your memory. In your pocket. Shared when you want.**

A serverless, in-process memory layer for AI agents. No servers, no web UI, no daemons. Just a Python library that gives agents a personal, searchable notebook with tiered context (L0/L1/L2), semantic search, and a self-improving review loop.

## Features

- **Zero infrastructure** — Runs in-process as a Python library. No servers, no HTTP, no daemons.
- **Tiered context** — L0 (abstract, ~50 tokens), L1 (overview, ~500 tokens), L2 (full detail, on-demand). 80-90% token reduction.
- **Hybrid retrieval** — Vector similarity (sqlite-vec) + keyword search (FTS5) with RRF fusion.
- **Personal + shared pools** — Each agent has a private vault; a shared Hermes-wide pool for cross-agent learning.
- **Self-improving review** — Agents annotate memories with confidence/verdicts; trust scores improve retrieval.
- **Local embeddings** — ONNX Runtime + all-MiniLM-L6-v2 int8 (23MB). No llama.cpp, no compilation, no GPU needed.
- **CLI for humans** — `mempalm stats/prune/export/review/backup/reembed`
- **Agent integrations** — Hermes MemoryProvider, MCP stdio tools, direct Python API

## Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Install
cd D:/projects/agent_palm
pip install -e .[dev]

# 2. Set your data directory (put it wherever you have space)
$env:MEMPALM_PATH = "D:\mempalm"

# 3. First memory
mempalm remember "Decided to use ONNX Runtime for embeddings - no more llama.cpp crashes!"

# 3. Search
mempalm search "embeddings" --max-tokens 500

# 4. Recall detail
mempalm recall "mem://personal/sebastian/default/note/abc123" --level l2

# 5. Stats
mempalm stats --pool both
```

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Agent Process (Hermes, Python script, etc.)                │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │  agent_palm.PalmPilot                                │    │
│  │  ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────┐ ┌────────┐  │    │
│  │  │  Store   │ │  Embed   │ │ Extract  │ │Retrieve│  │    │
│  │  │ (SQLite) │ │ (ONNX)   │ │ (Heuristic)│ │(RRF)   │  │    │
│  │  └──────────┘ └──────────┘ └──────────┘ └────────┘  │    │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            │
              ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
              ▼             ▼             ▼
         D:\mempalm\    D:\mempalm\    D:\mempalm\
         agents\         hermes.db      models\
         sebastian.db    (shared pool)  all-MiniLM-L6-v2_int8.onnx
         ling.db
```

## Tiered Context (L0/L1/L2)

| Level | Size | When Loaded | Purpose |
|-------|------|-------------|---------|
| **L0** | ~50 tokens | **Always** — every search result | Quick relevance check |
| **L1** | ~500 tokens | Until token budget fills | Key facts for reasoning |
| **L2** | Unlimited | **Explicit recall only** | Full detail when needed |

**Result:** 80-90% token reduction vs stuffing raw context.

## API

```python
from agent_palm import PalmPilot

palm = PalmPilot(agent_id="sebastian")

# Store a memory (auto-extracts L0/L1, embeds for search)
uri = palm.remember(
    "Decided to use ONNX Runtime for embeddings - no more llama.cpp crashes!",
    namespace="decisions",
    tags=["architecture", "embeddings"],
)

# Search with token budget
results = palm.search(
    "embedding crashes", 
    max_tokens=2000,  # Returns L0/L1 only
    pool="both"       # Search personal + shared
)

# Explicit full-detail recall
detail = palm.recall(uri, level="l2", max_tokens=4000)

# Self-improving review
palm.annotate(uri, "This decision was superseded by newer benchmarks", 
              confidence=0.9, verdict="superseded")
```

## Commands

```bash
# Store
mempalm remember "content" --namespace decisions --tags architecture,embeddings

# Search
mempalm search "embedding crashes" --max-tokens 2000 --pool both

# Recall
mempalm recall mem://personal/sebastian/... --level l2 --max-tokens 4000

# Stats
mempalm stats --namespace decisions --pool both

# Backup (safe, uses SQLite Backup API)
mempalm backup --destination D:\backups\mempalm_20241219

# Prune old memories
mempalm prune --older-than 90 --pool personal

# Export
mempalm export --namespace decisions --format jsonl > backup.jsonl
```

## Model

Default: **all-MiniLM-L6-v2 int8** (23MB, 384-dim, English-only)

For multilingual support, convert `multilingual-e5-small` to ONNX int8 and place in `D:\mempalm\models\`.

## Requirements

- Python 3.11+ (3.12/3.13 recommended for Windows)
- Windows 10/11, Linux, macOS
- No GPU required (CPU inference ~3-8ms per embed)
- ~200MB RAM (model + index + SQLite)

## Project Structure

```
agent_palm/
├── __init__.py          # Exports: PalmPilot, MemoryNode, MemoryRef, etc.
├── types.py             # Dataclasses: MemoryNode, MemoryRef, MemoryPool, etc.
├── exceptions.py        # PalmStorageBusyError, PalmModelMismatchError, etc.
├── schema.sql           # Single source of truth for DB schema
├── store.py             # PalmStore: SQLite + FTS5 + vec0, WAL, transactions
├── embed.py             # OnnxEmbedder (lazy) + HashEmbedder (tests)
├── extract.py           # Heuristic L0/L1 extraction
├── retrieval.py         # RRF fusion, budget packing, citation verification
├── review.py            # Annotations, trust, review queue (WIP)
├── hermes_provider.py   # Hermes MemoryProvider (WIP)
├── mcp_tool.py          # MCP stdio tools (WIP)
mempalm.py               # Click CLI: stats/prune/export/review/backup/reembed
pyproject.toml           # Dependencies: onnxruntime, tokenizers, sqlite-vec, numpy, click
schema.sql               # Source of truth for DB schema
policy.toml              # Shared pool permissions
tests/
    └── test_store.py    # Crash recovery, dedup, FTS, vec, backup, etc.
```

## Development

```bash
# Install dev dependencies
pip install -e .[dev]

# Run tests
pytest tests/ -v

# Run specific test
pytest tests/test_store.py::test_remember_and_recall -v

# Benchmark KNN
python -m benchmarks.bench_knn --nodes 100000 --dim 384 --runs 100
```

